## Method and sharpness

The proof includes equilibrium first variation, a nearest-support weak potential bound, Borel/measurable localization, and the layer-cake contradiction. Ordinary Borel Choquet capacitability and the capacity-zero/polar identification are explicit foundations, not the fine-topological Choquet property.

Precisely proved sharpness: decreasing the denominator exponent by any positive amount destroys the polar conclusion, and the exceptional set can be uncountable. No all-gauge optimality claim is made.

